It shall be unlawful for any owner of a domestic animal not to control the animal at all times through one of the following means:

- 1. Ona leash when off the property of the owner;

- 2. Within the passenger area of a vehicle driven or parked on the streets;

- 3. Within the property limits of its owner and attended by its owner; or

- 4. Confined within the property limits of its owner or of another with the permission of the person in control of the property. Any violation of this chapter will result in fines: 1* Offense of One Hundred Dollars ($100.00). 2™ Offense of One Hundred Fifty Dollars ($150.00). 3" Offense of Three Hundred Dollars ($300.00) and 30 days in jail for subsequent (court fees are not included in actual fine amount and will be added with each violation)
